## Behavioral Language Primitives

The following is a list of primitve that the engine can compute. Some of the entries have already been implemented, while others are simply a definition that will be implemented. The axiomatic and derived primitives perform transformations on the world. The context and invariant primitives establish the validity of the world. I am calling both primitives because they are indivisible semantic units that the behavioral language establishes but their actual function is different.

TODO: Revisit whether I am being too impresice with the use of the phrase primitive here. I think I established the distnction but maybe I am overloading the word. It doesn't affect the actual functionality, so I am deferring this to later.

These primitives are a declarative semantic rule that the engine can execute to derive the expected post-state, not an implementation of how the program performs the operation.

> [!IMPORTANT]  
> The list below is ongoing and will be populated as the Behavioral Language is defined further.

